WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.569
(gentle music)

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:09.008
- All right, Balazs, it's
good to see you again.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.276
- Hello, good to see you.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.910
- I think last time
I saw you in Florida

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.747 align:start size:97% position:3%
was about a year ago and
you welcomed me to Budapest,

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:18.417
you said, come on over to
Hungary, and here we are.

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:20.487 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Thank you very
much for visiting us.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:21.821
I hope you enjoy the weather.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.423
- Oh, well, I mean, the
weather is incredible.

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:27.026
The view, obviously, from
up here is incredible.

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:29.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
People will probably hear
a little construction

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:32.098
in the background, we are
sitting right across now

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.600
from the old Red Cross building,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.101
which is under construction.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.403
And I thought that
would be a nice way

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:37.771
to start the interview
because there is a lot

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.339 align:start size:84% position:16%
of construction going
on here, I mean,

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:42.675 align:start size:84% position:16%
this is an old city
that is, to me,

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.344
feeling a bit like a new city,

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
so there's something
interesting going on here.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.181
- Yes.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.483
I would add two things, one
is that, you know, it's a,

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.186
construction is always a
sign of economic success.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:57.757 align:start size:84% position:16%
So in general, if
you have construction
sites all over, you,

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:02.762
you know, probably, you don't
like them for a short period

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.732 align:start size:84% position:16%
of time, but for a
longer period of time,

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:09.201 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's like shows the economic
strengths of the country.

00:01:09.201 --> 00:01:12.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm happy to see
that here in Budapest is,

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.640 align:start size:88% position:13%
and all around Hungary,
something is doing.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.842
And the other part
is reconstruction

00:01:16.842 --> 00:01:21.614 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the so-called
Buda Castle Hill and,

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:25.752 align:start size:97% position:3%
which was actually demolished
in the Second World War,

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:29.355 align:start size:97% position:3%
it was bombed by the Russians,
and then before that,

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:33.860
it was used for military
operation by the Nazis.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.363 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then the Hungarian
communists, who
obviously occupied

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:41.067
the country, they also
did some serious damage.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:44.704
And these used to be classical,

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.873 align:start size:88% position:13%
wonderful architectural
style buildings,

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:50.910 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we made the decision
to rebuild them.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.847
It's like there is a
governmental program,

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.349
so if you come back in two
years' time, you will see

00:01:56.349 --> 00:02:00.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
the entire cast here fully
recovered, everything

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:04.224 align:start size:97% position:3%
is rebuilding in beautiful
classical architectural style,

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.561
it's still the best,
it's right now, today,

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.596 align:start size:84% position:16%
is the one of the
best places of Europe,

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:13.533 align:start size:88% position:13%
but it's gonna be
really, really gorgeous.

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.002
- Yeah, and as you
know, I'm coming here

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.704
after a nine-day trip to Israel,

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.971
and one of the things
that I found there

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:22.808
is they're constantly in
this battle between old

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:26.345 align:start position:0%
and tradition and new and
technology and everything else.

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:28.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems like something
similar is happening here,

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.384
that you guys are trying
to look back at your past,

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.385
figure out the good parts
to bring to the future,

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:36.689
but then also govern in
a somewhat sensible way,

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.292
which is pretty rare for
the West at the moment.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.560 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You're not anymore
talking about architecture.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.596 align:start size:97% position:3%
- No, we're not talking about,
well, we can if you want,

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:47.000
are they gonna be putting up
some modern buildings here?

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.969
- Oh, actually, but,
you know, this is,

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:54.340
from the architecture debate,
you can understand, actually,

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.610
everything, because what we
are doing here is that we try

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:02.281 align:start position:0%
to restore everything which
made Hungary great in the past.

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:06.052
And it's part of our heritage,
if we are not proud of that,

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.655
then what makes us Hungarians,

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.390
what is the purpose of our life?

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.191
So this is the important part.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:15.094 align:start size:88% position:13%
And the other part is
you will see in the city

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:20.166 align:start size:97% position:3%
some other modern buildings
which were created

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.769
by foreigners, very
famous architects

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:25.537
from all over the world.

00:03:25.537 --> 00:03:28.407
I think it gives
us pride as well

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:32.545
to bring them to Hungary
and let them to work here.

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:37.250 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we are fighting against
the modern concrete and glass.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:45.225
I mean, just like nothing
special type of buildings.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:49.995 align:start size:97% position:3%
If there is something
Hungarian in that, obviously,

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:51.764 align:start size:84% position:16%
it has to be a
high quality thing,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:56.836 align:start position:0%
but has to add some tiny
little Hungarian thing in that,

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.806 align:start size:84% position:16%
this is how the things
are going to work.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:03.475 align:start position:0%
And not only in just
architecture and reconstruction,

00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:06.712 align:start size:97% position:3%
but like policy making, family
policy, things like that-

00:04:06.712 --> 00:04:09.315 align:start size:88% position:13%
- How do you think those
things are connected?

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:12.385
Like architecture and
actually city life

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:14.620
and physically what
you're looking at

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.889
to the political side of things?

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:21.761
- I think that, you know, to
figure out what the people want

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:26.632
and what makes to be a good
government, it's not so hard.

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:29.201
Obviously, you can learn
about this for like years

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:34.274
in universities, but you get
the point very, very easily.

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:39.945
Like people want a safe
and beautiful environment

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:43.015 align:start size:97% position:3%
around them, people want a
very, a supportive environment

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:48.087 align:start position:0%
around them, a state which
helps them to raise their kids,

00:04:48.887 --> 00:04:51.090
to make a family, to have jobs.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.059
They want secure streets,

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:57.563
they don't want garbage
all around everywhere.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:05:02.568
They want companies which are
producing high quality goods,

00:05:03.969 --> 00:05:07.005
so it's so simple and you
are having good government

00:05:07.005 --> 00:05:11.944
if you see that things
slowly, unfortunately,

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.179
but go into that direction.

00:05:14.179 --> 00:05:15.981
If you look back
retrospectively,

00:05:15.981 --> 00:05:19.252
it's obvious then where
you were 10 years ago

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.487
and what did you
achieve since then,

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:24.223
and if you see this
kind of progress,

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:27.960 align:start size:88% position:13%
not the progressive
ideology, then you feel

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.229
that something good
is happening, if not,

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.598
then you have to change
course because otherwise,

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.833
you're going down.

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.901
- What do you think the
secret to the success

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:38.304
of that has been in Hungary,
now, obviously, you're a rough,

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.273 align:start size:88% position:13%
you're a fairly small
country population-wise,

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:41.940
only about 10 million people.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.143 align:start size:84% position:16%
So there's an ability,
it seems to me,

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:46.979
to direct those people
in a certain way where,

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:50.182 align:start size:97% position:3%
from an American perspective,
350 million people,

00:05:50.182 --> 00:05:53.319 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's harder to herd those
cats and get them to see that,

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:54.853
we're seeing it at
the state level.

00:05:54.853 --> 00:05:56.455
Since I've been here, we've
talked a lot about Florida,

00:05:56.455 --> 00:06:00.092
you know, that's working, but
the national project seems

00:06:00.092 --> 00:06:00.960
to be struggling.

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:08.033 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I think the most important
thing that you have

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:11.604
to be sure and make
sure that the people,

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:14.740
grassroot voters,
are behind you.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:15.975
And then it doesn't matter

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.843
whether the media is
going against you,

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:20.779 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether the big corporations
are going against you.

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:24.617 align:start position:0%
In our case, as a small country,
international organization,

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:29.689
NGOs, and like Brussels
is going against us.

00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:33.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if the people are
backing what we are doing,

00:06:33.258 --> 00:06:36.829
then we are fine, this will
be always the last frontier,

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:40.265
the last, you know,
just place to stand.

00:06:40.265 --> 00:06:41.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Do you find that people
like that, actually,

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:43.669
that the people support you more

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:46.872
when Brussels comes after
you or if you take a, say,

00:06:46.872 --> 00:06:48.941 align:start size:84% position:16%
an immigration
policy that obviously

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:51.577
is counter to what the EU is
doing, that sort of thing?

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.579
- Honestly, among us,
I don't understand

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:56.348 align:start position:0%
why they are doing that, because
the more pressure they put

00:06:56.348 --> 00:06:59.518 align:start size:97% position:3%
on us, the, the more popular
we are getting in Hungary

00:06:59.518 --> 00:07:00.686
because it's obvious-

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:01.621
- Yeah, yeah.

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:03.422
- I mean, what happened in 2015,

00:07:03.422 --> 00:07:07.660
400 people made the decision
to march across the country

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.363
without any kind of permission.

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:15.501 align:start position:0%
It's like not good, it's against
the idea of law and order,

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:17.903 align:start size:84% position:16%
people want to
have law and order.

00:07:17.903 --> 00:07:22.141 align:start size:97% position:3%
So they said that they support
the government to stop it.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:24.810
And since we have the attacks,

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:28.681 align:start position:0%
they support the government
even more, with a bigger metric.

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:31.484 align:start position:0%
It's actually not a
controversial issue politically

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:32.918
in Hungary.

00:07:32.918 --> 00:07:36.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also, if you ask the
leftist opposition voters

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:39.525 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether they support
stricter immigration policy,

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:41.760 align:start size:84% position:16%
their answer answer
would be yes.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:45.163
- So what is going on
with the left here?

00:07:45.163 --> 00:07:47.600
It seems to me that
maybe it's not quite

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:51.236
as radical as our left,
is that fair to say?

00:07:51.236 --> 00:07:53.672 align:start size:97% position:3%
I've asked a few people
that over the last day or so

00:07:53.672 --> 00:07:56.375 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I'm getting
various, they wanna be?

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:57.310
- They want to be there-

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:58.544
- Well, that means they're not,

00:07:58.544 --> 00:07:59.645
so it's probably
pretty good, yeah.

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:00.880
- That's it, excuse me.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:05.050
- Well, you know, we
were talking about it.

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:10.122 align:start position:0%
I think the general
environment, it does matter, so,

00:08:11.256 --> 00:08:15.160
and this is the reason
why the responsibility

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.897
of the media is big.

00:08:17.897 --> 00:08:21.433
So I mean, it's like
politics is one issue,

00:08:21.433 --> 00:08:24.303
party political debates
are part of democracy,

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:26.772
it's like, it's not about that.

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:29.208 align:start size:84% position:16%
But there is a common,
there should be

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:33.378 align:start position:0%
at least a common understanding
that, for example,

00:08:33.378 --> 00:08:38.017
you do not support any
kind of violation at all.

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:46.125
And the media should not
support that, full stop,

00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:48.561
this is based on common sense,

00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:51.697
not based on party
political ideas.

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:54.567
And in Hungary,
I think the media

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:58.638
and even some serious
opposition parties,

00:08:58.638 --> 00:09:00.906 align:start size:84% position:16%
they take it seriously
because they see,

00:09:00.906 --> 00:09:03.609
if they go to another direction,

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:05.811 align:start size:84% position:16%
then the voters,
they will punish them

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:09.114 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they will not support
them anymore, they will look

00:09:09.114 --> 00:09:12.851 align:start size:97% position:3%
for other alternative,
probably they will not vote

00:09:12.851 --> 00:09:14.687
for Fidesz, but
they were looking

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:17.222 align:start size:84% position:16%
for new alternatives
on the left.

00:09:17.222 --> 00:09:18.157
- Do you sense that-

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:19.691
- I'm happy to experience that.

00:09:19.691 --> 00:09:22.962
- Yeah, no, I wish we had
a little bit more of that

00:09:22.962 --> 00:09:24.863 align:start size:88% position:13%
with our left, it would
help bring balance-

00:09:24.863 --> 00:09:26.298
- It's this fear
of radicalization,

00:09:26.298 --> 00:09:28.334
you have to somehow
be able to stop it.

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:29.601 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, it's
interesting because,

00:09:29.601 --> 00:09:32.605 align:start size:84% position:16%
from an American
perspective, our left,

00:09:32.605 --> 00:09:34.573
they can have different
policies, obviously,

00:09:34.573 --> 00:09:36.342 align:start size:88% position:13%
but there's something
else where they're angry

00:09:36.342 --> 00:09:37.643
at the founding of the nation,

00:09:37.643 --> 00:09:39.678
they're angry at the
laws of the nation.

00:09:39.678 --> 00:09:42.014
That strikes me as much
more dangerous where-

00:09:43.615 --> 00:09:48.220
- That's the thing when we
start talking about the LGBTQ

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:57.296
and the gender issues, and the
pope was here two weeks ago,

00:09:58.397 --> 00:10:00.499
CPAC was here one
week ago, actually,

00:10:00.499 --> 00:10:03.569 align:start size:88% position:13%
since the Pope was here,
that's when we have,

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:05.404
since then, we have
the good weather, so.

00:10:05.404 --> 00:10:06.639
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:07.673
Well, then he did
something right.

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:08.674
- He did something.

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:13.745
And everybody was
very clear on that,

00:10:13.745 --> 00:10:18.084 align:start size:97% position:3%
that this kind of gender
ideology, it's very dangerous

00:10:18.084 --> 00:10:21.253
because it divides the nation.

00:10:21.253 --> 00:10:26.325
So it wants to override
the idea of nationhood

00:10:27.125 --> 00:10:28.327
and of that all the people,

00:10:28.327 --> 00:10:29.662 align:start size:84% position:16%
it doesn't matter
what color they have,

00:10:29.662 --> 00:10:31.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
how old are they,
where are they from,

00:10:31.964 --> 00:10:34.467 align:start position:0%
they belong to the same
nation, and there is more thing

00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:38.671
which unites them than
brings them separately.

00:10:38.671 --> 00:10:43.643
So, and if you let these
ideologies emerge, then,

00:10:45.344 --> 00:10:48.681 align:start size:97% position:3%
at the end of the day, sooner
or later, it takes years,

00:10:48.681 --> 00:10:50.783
but it will destroy everything

00:10:50.783 --> 00:10:52.051
which brings the
people together,

00:10:52.051 --> 00:10:55.788
and then it will be
very hard to maintain

00:10:55.788 --> 00:11:00.392 align:start position:0%
and to manage even the most
basic functions of the society.

00:11:00.392 --> 00:11:03.495 align:start position:0%
- Yeah, it was interesting
because when I spoke last night,

00:11:03.495 --> 00:11:06.932
I mentioned how, you know,
there should be a separation

00:11:06.932 --> 00:11:10.169
between the LG and B
and T, that the T thing

00:11:10.169 --> 00:11:13.739
is actually anti-LG and
B and it's anti-women.

00:11:13.739 --> 00:11:15.874
And it got a nice round of
applause, which I was happy

00:11:15.874 --> 00:11:17.376 align:start size:84% position:16%
to hear from a
conservative audience,

00:11:17.376 --> 00:11:21.313
because I think that that's
an important part to note.

00:11:21.313 --> 00:11:26.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
- True, but like, but also
in the migration issue

00:11:28.687 --> 00:11:33.759 align:start size:97% position:3%
and with the, in general, with
the sexual minority issues,

00:11:35.026 --> 00:11:39.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously, discrimination
is not acceptable

00:11:39.431 --> 00:11:43.569 align:start size:97% position:3%
because we are the same
society, all are human beings.

00:11:43.569 --> 00:11:47.006 align:start position:0%
Any kind of sexual
discrimination is unacceptable.

00:11:47.006 --> 00:11:50.009
Now, what we are doing in
Hungary is we try to focus

00:11:51.377 --> 00:11:53.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
on what things are
bringing together people.

00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:58.884
The wealthy people, the
not so wealthy people,

00:11:58.884 --> 00:12:01.219
the young people,
the old people,

00:12:01.219 --> 00:12:04.657 align:start size:97% position:3%
people coming from different
parts of the country.

00:12:04.657 --> 00:12:07.693 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you have to
put a lot of energy

00:12:07.693 --> 00:12:11.696 align:start size:88% position:13%
into convincing the
society that it's worth

00:12:11.696 --> 00:12:14.833
to keep together, if we
have national purposes,

00:12:14.833 --> 00:12:19.137
then we have to, you
know, keep united.

00:12:19.137 --> 00:12:22.708 align:start position:0%
And I think this is what I
learned from the United States.

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:24.610 align:start size:88% position:13%
This is how your
wonderful country became

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:26.711
the most successful
country on Earth.

00:12:26.711 --> 00:12:29.481
- Right, and interestingly, I
mean, the purpose of this trip

00:12:29.481 --> 00:12:32.351 align:start size:88% position:13%
for me was to figure out
how do I import maybe

00:12:32.351 --> 00:12:35.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
what is going on here back
into the United States,

00:12:35.621 --> 00:12:37.656 align:start size:88% position:13%
because we seem to have
lost a lot of that,

00:12:37.656 --> 00:12:39.224
what would be your main message?

00:12:39.224 --> 00:12:41.192
I mean, you've been to
the United States a ton,

00:12:41.192 --> 00:12:43.662 align:start size:97% position:3%
you were actually in Florida
just a couple weeks ago.

00:12:43.662 --> 00:12:46.799
I mean, when you see some
of what's going on there,

00:12:46.799 --> 00:12:48.267
what would be your main message

00:12:48.267 --> 00:12:51.070 align:start size:81% position:19%
on how to fix some
of this stuff?

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:54.673
- Well, first of all,
we know our place.

00:12:54.673 --> 00:12:59.478
So it's still a small,
small country far away

00:12:59.478 --> 00:13:04.383
from the United States after
many centuries of suffering.

00:13:05.751 --> 00:13:08.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
So how, you know, it's the
mouse and the elephant,

00:13:08.387 --> 00:13:10.322 align:start size:88% position:13%
should I give an
advice to the elephant?

00:13:10.322 --> 00:13:14.260
So I don't think that
it should be cured.

00:13:15.594 --> 00:13:20.399
But our experience is that
people want to fix their life

00:13:24.569 --> 00:13:27.006
and people want to
fix their country.

00:13:28.307 --> 00:13:32.845 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, and it's not impossible
to bring them together

00:13:34.079 --> 00:13:36.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be united, especially
in a democracy,

00:13:36.114 --> 00:13:39.752 align:start size:84% position:16%
democracy is still the
best form to do so.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:46.192
And all politicians who want
to restore American greatness

00:13:47.593 --> 00:13:51.196
or do something against what
is going on right now there

00:13:51.196 --> 00:13:52.897
should be aware
of the fact that,

00:13:52.897 --> 00:13:55.568 align:start size:97% position:3%
if the people are behind you,
you have to convince them

00:13:55.568 --> 00:13:58.270
to be on board with
you, and then you

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.972 align:start size:84% position:16%
will have the chance
to bring change.

00:14:00.972 --> 00:14:03.608
- And do you basically just
ignore all of the noise?

00:14:03.608 --> 00:14:04.943
I mean, the Prime
Minister's office

00:14:04.943 --> 00:14:07.112
is literally about
30 feet that way,

00:14:07.112 --> 00:14:09.681
I don't think he's in the
building at the moment but,

00:14:09.681 --> 00:14:12.117
you know, when I tweet
that I'm coming here

00:14:12.117 --> 00:14:13.885
or I retweet you, I get
a certain amount of,

00:14:13.885 --> 00:14:15.854
oh, it's fascist
and they're mean

00:14:15.854 --> 00:14:17.456 align:start size:84% position:16%
and blah, blah, blah,
and I look at it

00:14:17.456 --> 00:14:19.324
and I then I just keep
meeting pleasant people

00:14:19.324 --> 00:14:21.960
and seeing what's actually
happening on the ground.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:24.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I mean, do you just
basically ignore the noise

00:14:24.262 --> 00:14:25.231
and just go ahead?

00:14:26.599 --> 00:14:31.136 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I mean, I would be surprised
if they were supporting me,

00:14:32.304 --> 00:14:35.641
so that would cause us
more problem, I think-

00:14:35.641 --> 00:14:38.077 align:start size:97% position:3%
- If the media was supporting
you, that would, yeah,

00:14:38.077 --> 00:14:39.611
that's what DeSantis says also-

00:14:39.611 --> 00:14:41.079
- Would support us.

00:14:41.079 --> 00:14:42.881
- Yeah, well, it was a
pleasure seeing you again

00:14:42.881 --> 00:14:47.953 align:start position:0%
and I look forward to
exploring just this absolutely,

00:14:49.321 --> 00:14:50.656
tell me one, yeah, give me
one thing that we should do

00:14:50.656 --> 00:14:52.123
if we have a little
fresh time today.

00:14:52.123 --> 00:14:53.658 align:start size:97% position:3%
- This is the Hungarian
Empire Parliament Building-

00:14:53.658 --> 00:14:55.093
- Absolutely stunning.

00:14:55.093 --> 00:14:56.695 align:start size:81% position:19%
- It's a gorgeous,
gorgeous thing,

00:14:56.695 --> 00:15:01.700 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it's about
Hungarian sovereignty

00:15:03.034 --> 00:15:07.473
because it was built more
than 120-30 years ago.

00:15:08.574 --> 00:15:11.309
And back at the time,
there was a competition

00:15:11.309 --> 00:15:13.045 align:start size:84% position:16%
among the architects
that what kind

00:15:13.045 --> 00:15:15.547
of building should be built.

00:15:15.547 --> 00:15:19.651 align:start size:97% position:3%
And there was a commission
which made the final decision.

00:15:19.651 --> 00:15:23.322 align:start size:97% position:3%
And as you see, this is
the only neo-Gothical style

00:15:23.322 --> 00:15:25.423
of building in town,
all the other ones

00:15:25.423 --> 00:15:29.594
are just now neoclassical and
neo-Renaissance buildings.

00:15:29.594 --> 00:15:32.931
And back at that time,
the commission was saying

00:15:32.931 --> 00:15:38.003
that it cannot happen that the
Hungarian Parliament building

00:15:39.538 --> 00:15:41.640
will have the same
architectural style

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:44.309 align:start size:84% position:16%
as the Vienna
government buildings

00:15:44.309 --> 00:15:46.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they were
neo-Renaissance buildings.

00:15:46.377 --> 00:15:49.448 align:start size:97% position:3%
So that's the reason why
they went to that direction,

00:15:49.448 --> 00:15:52.150
because they wanted to
have an independent,

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:54.553 align:start size:84% position:16%
a different, a
sovereign decision,

00:15:54.553 --> 00:15:56.755
so they were choosing this kind

00:15:56.755 --> 00:15:59.357 align:start size:84% position:16%
of neo-Gothical
architecture style,

00:15:59.357 --> 00:16:01.994
there are no other buildings
with this style in the country,

00:16:01.994 --> 00:16:04.897 align:start size:84% position:16%
this is the only one,
and this is like,

00:16:04.897 --> 00:16:08.367
even 130 years ago, the
most important thing

00:16:08.367 --> 00:16:10.369 align:start size:84% position:16%
for Hungarian people
was sovereignty,

00:16:10.369 --> 00:16:15.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
how they differentiate the
Hungarians from Vienna,

00:16:18.243 --> 00:16:22.014
which was the headquarter of
the empire back at that time.

00:16:22.014 --> 00:16:24.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
So if you come to Hungary,
you will see a lot

00:16:24.949 --> 00:16:30.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
of tiny little signs,
people for like 1000 year

00:16:31.156 --> 00:16:33.359
or even more fighting
for their sovereignty.

00:16:33.359 --> 00:16:35.894 align:start size:84% position:16%
And this is, if
you see the result,

00:16:35.894 --> 00:16:39.064
this is a fight which
was to be continued.

00:16:39.064 --> 00:16:41.166 align:start size:97% position:3%
- And on the continuing
path, you will also see a lot

00:16:41.166 --> 00:16:43.502
of cranes because there's a
lot of new things going up.

00:16:43.502 --> 00:16:46.405
So that proves it
right there, right-

00:16:46.405 --> 00:16:49.007 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Is the basilica, which
is the main church,

00:16:49.007 --> 00:16:51.610
the parliament building,
and the soccer stadium.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.078
So these are the-

00:16:53.078 --> 00:16:54.780 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It's all here.
- This is a triangle.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:55.880
- It was great to
see you, my friend.

